{
 "note": "Mutants of the owner's accounts (src/ants_server/admin_accounts.cpp, admin_cli.cpp, the owner's part of submissions_http.cpp, crypto.cpp's PBKDF2 and comparison, the version 6 migration) for tools/mutate.py (docs/TESTING.md). Run from the checkout with a configured build folder: python3 tools/mutate.py tests/data/admin_accounts_mutants.json --keep-going --jobs 1 --timeout 900. Every mutant must be caught: each breaks one rule of docs/MAP_SUBMISSIONS.md, 'Accounts' (the hash and its cost, a comparison that looks at every byte, the work an unknown name costs, the three limits on guessing to the try and the second, the budget of password checks, the generation of the sessions, the last Admin, the roles and the answer for a Moderator, the forced change of a starting password, the cookie's flags and time, CSRF and the sign-in's checks, the log, the migration). Not listed on purpose, because no program can tell them apart from the real one: a password longer than 256 bytes that is refused before any work (a hash of it would be refused anyway) and the zeroing of a password in memory (not done).",
